Anatomy Mirror derived meshes
Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 2.1 Japan (CC BY-SA 2.1 JP)

The bone meshes and the brain shell in anatomy.glb are adapted from
BodyParts3D / Anatomography, copyright Database Center for Life Science (DBCLS).
BodyParts3D is licensed under CC BY-SA 2.1 Japan:
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.1/jp/deed.en

You may copy, share, and adapt these meshes provided you give credit, link the
licence, and distribute adaptations under the same licence.

The five muscle shapes (frontalis, corrugator supercilii, orbicularis oculi,
zygomaticus major, masseter) are original schematic surfaces made for this app,
because BodyParts3D release 4.3 does not contain those muscles. They are included
in anatomy.glb and released under the same CC BY-SA 2.1 Japan licence so the
file has one licence.

The canonical face coordinates used only to align the meshes come from the
MediaPipe canonical face model (Apache License 2.0).
